WEBVTT

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:55.000
Welcome to this collection of some of the finest natural history films ever made.

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:59.810
Each volume in the series will give you an intimate view of many of the most...

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.280
and remarkable creatures which inhabit our planet.

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:05.460
Month by month, more titles will be released

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:08.260
so that it will build into a unique collection,

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:10.360
something to treasure for years to come.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:14.680
Watch out for other titles in the series after the films which follow.

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:55.730
We surround ourselves with animals that we love and sometimes we bring them from distant

00:01:55.730 --> 00:01:59.670
parts of the world, so we tend to forget how they looked and lived.

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:06.400
in their original homes the budgerigar the most popular of these pets comes from the

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:28.800
outback of australia the peacock from the plains of india here they are this is the tale of two

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:29.980
very different creatures

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:33.630
but two whose stories are intimately entwined.

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:36.510
It's the tale of the peacock and the tiger.

00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:06.150
In Britain, peacocks are exotic ornaments to stately homes.

00:03:09.190 --> 00:03:13.610
Spacious lawns provide a stage for the cocks to flaunt their bejeweled tales

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:17.070
at an audience of drab and admiring peahens.

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:22.880
But peafowl aren't native to Britain, or even to Europe,

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:26.020
though they've been known here since the 14th century.

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:29.980
They've long been valued for the splendor of the cocks' magnitudes.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:40.210
magnificent tail. But how did the peacock get its tail? For the answer to that, we must go to its homeland, to India.

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:47.590
Here, the peacock has more ancient links with man. Its images are set in stone,

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:55.120
portrayed in paint. Today, the deserted palaces of Mughal emperors and Rajput princes are

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:59.780
embellished by the living, but these are no pampered ornaments.

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:07.380
They're truly wild, and despite the apparent handicap of the male's enormous tail, they can and do fly.

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:16.300
The peacock is modern India's national bird, but its place in the national psyche has far

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:17.240
older roots.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:24.100
Wild creatures of all kinds are embodied in India's folklore and religious beliefs.

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:29.880
In the Hindu pantheon, langur monkeys are identified with Hanuman, the monkey.

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:42.610
peacocks too are venerated but monkeys are no respecters of divinity when there's food to be had

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:57.810
the peacocks have to wait their turn peacock was the mount of Kartika the god of war maybe

00:05:57.810 --> 00:05:59.750
because the bird has a legendary ability

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:05.780
to destroy snakes perhaps for that reason peacocks are seldom killed so they're

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:15.700
often found in Indian villages the bird's prolific breeding has made it a

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:19.880
symbol of fertility and the dancing of the peacock is said to foretell the

00:06:19.880 --> 00:06:29.770
coming of the rains a momentous event in this dry and hungry land the links

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.320
between man and peacock, go back over 2,000 years.

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:36.840
But the bird itself is far older than that.

00:06:37.260 --> 00:06:40.080
To solve the riddle of how the peacock got its tail,

00:06:40.280 --> 00:06:43.300
we must go to the jungle, to its wild neighbors.

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:49.000
This is another world, a world of hunters and hunted,

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:52.300
where constant vigilance is the price of life.

00:06:56.860 --> 00:06:59.840
Queen among hunters is the cat that walks by.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:06.960
himself, the steed of the goddess Kali, the destroyer, the tiger. Almost all the jungle's

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:29.110
creatures have reason to fear him. Peacock or Samba deer, the tiger is lord of all he surveys.

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:33.030
And he hunts alone.

00:07:35.370 --> 00:07:39.930
He must remain hidden, for paradoxically, the peacock has the power to ruin his hunt.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:30.260
June.

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:33.040
in the sun-scorched hills of Rajasthan.

00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:34.880
the height of the dry season.

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:37.800
There's been almost no rain for nine months.

00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:53.550
Peacock's day starts early.

00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:06.960
At this season, the males are in their full splendour.

00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:09.640
Cocks don't carry their tails all year.

00:09:10.170 --> 00:09:12.070
They lose them in the annual moat.

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:16.340
And it takes several weeks for that bespangled train to grow anew.

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:24.380
all life is now concentrated around the few dwindling water holes.

00:09:25.110 --> 00:09:27.750
the peacock's rain dance has yet to have its effect.

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:47.180
Sooner or later, all the jungle creatures must come here to drink.

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:48.740
Samba

00:09:49.290 --> 00:09:50.390
and the Dapu Chi Tao.

00:09:53.350 --> 00:09:54.630
bristly wild pig.

00:09:57.290 --> 00:09:59.610
And the strangely misshapen Nilgai antelope.

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:08.180
For the monkeys, the peacock and the deer, this is the leanest time of year.

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:13.900
Tiger is the fattest.

00:10:15.410 --> 00:10:17.530
All his subjects are now gathered before him.

00:10:18.020 --> 00:10:20.760
He can afford to wait and to choose.

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:29.880
Peacocks come early to the water.

00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:30.330
home.

00:10:32.460 --> 00:10:34.760
The first arrivals, jockey for position.

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:46.960
Cocks are sparring for a patch of ground to call their own.

00:11:06.940 --> 00:11:07.220
this

00:11:07.580 --> 00:11:08.100
is why.

00:11:09.110 --> 00:11:13.490
As the morning wears on, a steady stream of peahens fly in to drink.

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:20.190
All the hens in the neighbourhood must come here each morning, there can be a hundred or more.

00:11:37.640 --> 00:11:40.420
For any male that wants to pull the birds...

00:11:40.620 --> 00:11:43.500
this watering hole is clearly a good place to be.

00:11:44.710 --> 00:11:46.210
and it's a good place for hunters.

00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:47.600
of another kind.

00:11:57.740 --> 00:11:59.760
Cocks spend a lot of their time fighting.

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:03.420
Could this be one reason for having such a splendid tale?

00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:10.940
It may not impress a tiger.

00:12:11.350 --> 00:12:14.050
But does the tale intimidate rival males?

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:20.810
It seems not.

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:24.060
The full display is reserved for the pea hens.

00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:27.500
The cocks are fighting for a space to thraunt their tails,

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:29.780
like boys jostling for the best seat.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:31.620
bar to chat up the girls.

00:12:34.470 --> 00:12:37.570
Any peahen coming to the waterhole can take her pick.

00:12:37.930 --> 00:12:40.050
from the strutting and posturing cocks.

00:12:40.840 --> 00:12:44.640
But, as in any rough pub, you can be knocked off your barstool.

00:12:47.050 --> 00:12:49.590
So could this be the reason for the peacock's tail?

00:12:50.150 --> 00:12:52.590
Do hens prefer males with big tails?

00:13:06.740 --> 00:13:08.560
The answer seems to be yes.

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:14.560
Careful observation has shown that peahens select the cocks with the most eye spots in their tails.

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:19.450
that doesn't mean

00:13:19.680 --> 00:13:21.280
They actually count the spots.

00:13:21.590 --> 00:13:26.550
there can be over 200, it's probably the overall impact of the display that matters.

00:13:28.380 --> 00:13:29.960
It's even been suggested that all

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:34.200
those eyes hypnotize the female into submission. Whatever the reason,

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:37.150
Peahens certainly seem to have an eye for beauty.

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:41.660
But what's so good about it?

00:13:41.700 --> 00:13:43.260
peacocks with big tails.

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:50.540
Very recently, it's been found that the offspring of males with the most elaborate tails grow and survive better.

00:13:50.940 --> 00:13:56.900
And if tail size is inherited, it makes even more sense for a hen to choose the most spectacular cock.

00:13:57.580 --> 00:14:00.000
By doing so, she's giving her sons...

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:01.760
the best possible start in life.

00:14:06.010 --> 00:14:09.310
It's three years before a peacock can grow a full tail.

00:14:10.040 --> 00:14:12.360
The weakest males may not live that long.

00:14:13.140 --> 00:14:15.060
This young cock's doing his best.

00:14:15.670 --> 00:14:17.050
but he leaves the hands cold.

00:14:30.660 --> 00:14:36.300
If peahens prefer males with flamboyant tails, and if that trait is passed on to their young,

00:14:36.840 --> 00:14:39.300
What stops the tail getting bigger and bigger?

00:14:41.320 --> 00:14:41.620
That?

00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:44.000
is where the tiger comes into this parable.

00:14:49.830 --> 00:14:52.970
Big tails could be handicapped in all sorts of ways.

00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:54.800
like deer's antlers.

00:14:55.050 --> 00:14:57.050
They have to be grown anew each year.

00:14:57.380 --> 00:14:58.340
And that takes energy.

00:14:59.210 --> 00:14:59.950
There are a lot of...

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:01.040
to carry around.

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:04.480
That must make the bearer slower, less agile.

00:15:05.080 --> 00:15:06.400
easier prey for hunters.

00:15:07.210 --> 00:15:07.390
Thank you.

00:15:12.700 --> 00:15:15.820
In the dry season, the tiger is spoiled for choice.

00:15:17.110 --> 00:15:18.170
Will he pick a pig?

00:15:18.740 --> 00:15:19.400
Peacock

00:15:19.770 --> 00:15:21.090
Chitao o Samba.

00:15:21.720 --> 00:15:23.340
or must run the gauntlet.

00:15:23.930 --> 00:15:24.930
or die of thirst.

00:16:47.980 --> 00:16:48.320
time.

00:16:48.710 --> 00:16:49.990
A cheetah was unlucky.

00:16:50.730 --> 00:16:51.910
there's more meat on the deer

00:16:52.300 --> 00:16:52.960
and a peacock.

00:17:06.810 --> 00:17:08.610
There's still no end to the drought.

00:17:09.300 --> 00:17:11.740
The monsoon rains are no more than a promise.

00:17:12.730 --> 00:17:16.070
Daytime temperatures rise to 45 degrees or more.

00:17:16.820 --> 00:17:18.080
every patch of shade.

00:17:18.420 --> 00:17:20.400
Every pool of water is precious.

00:17:39.750 --> 00:17:42.330
All have their own way of keeping cool.

00:17:57.860 --> 00:17:59.280
For most of the jungle's creatures,

00:17:59.850 --> 00:17:59.970
Thank you.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:01.940
This is a cruel time of the year.

00:18:04.250 --> 00:18:04.410
Thank you.

00:18:06.200 --> 00:18:07.140
Only for the tiger.

00:18:07.580 --> 00:18:08.960
Is it a season of ease?

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:11.050
though his sleep

